# 1-based lines to bookmark. Each sits INSIDE a construct the profile claims to
# understand, so a broken `containers` shows up as a missing breadcrumb.
#
# Lines are chosen to be structurally distinct from their siblings. Codemark
# refuses a bookmark whose generated query matches more than one node, so a
# statement with an identically-shaped sibling is not a usable anchor (the
# Scala profile hit exactly this).

# Inside a loop inside a conditional inside a method inside a class:
# class Invoice > compute > for (const line of ...) > if (line.amount === 0).
# The deepest control-flow chain; `continue` is the only one in the file.
84

# Inside an arrow function inside a method: Invoice > discounted > (amount) =>.
# Proves an arrow_function body is reachable. Unlike Python's lambda or Rust's
# closure, this one the generator *does* propose — an arrow function has a
# body, so it is observable from the samples.
97

# Inside a static method inside a class: class Invoice > static count().
128

# Inside a function nested in a function: build > toLine.
# Proves function-in-function containment.
139

# Inside a method on an object literal, inside a function:
# build > helpers = { sum() }. A method_definition outside any class.
145
